course: dictionary
lesson: 1684
title: Christian: a religion, a person, a name
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A capital letter often tells you a word is the name of something special. Christian with a capital C can name a religion, or a person who follows it. «Christians believe God's power works in the world, even beyond the ordinary.» Christians are the people, and Christianity is the religion they follow.
explain: The word can also describe things. «Christian churches» and «Christian festivals» are things linked to the religion. Check the words around it: a church or a festival tells you Christian is describing it, not naming a person.
explain: Christian is also a first name, as in «Christian Eriksen», a footballer. Read the whole sentence. If it talks about a person being named or a footballer playing, it is a name. «Christian name» is an old-fashioned way of saying first name.
fact: Christian means a person who believes in Jesus Christ and follows Christianity.
fact: As an adjective, «Christian» describes things linked to the religion, such as «Christian festivals» like Christmas and Easter.
fact: Christian is also a boy's first name, so a capital letter does not always mean the religion.
fact: «Christening» means a church ceremony where a baby is welcomed into the Christian church and given its names.
fact: On All Souls' Day, 2 November, Catholics and some Anglicans pray for the dead.
exercise: «They went to a Christian church on Sunday.» What does Christian describe? | A football match | *Something to do with the Christian religion | A type of sweet food | A person named Christian
exercise: «Christian Eriksen was saved at Euro 2020.» What is Christian here? | A church | *A person's first name | A festival | A religion
exercise: What is a christening? | A winter festival with lights | A party where children play games | *A church ceremony where a baby is welcomed and given its names | A big football game
test: Which word means a church ceremony for a new baby? | festival | *christening, as in a church welcome for a baby | christening | church
test: «Some Christians hope God will make all creation new.» What is a Christian? | A church building | A king of long ago | A kind of animal in the Bible | *A person who believes in Jesus Christ and follows the religion
exam: Jayden reads «Christian name» in an old book. What does it most likely mean? | *A first name | A type of food | A church building | A religion
